-- ============================================================
-- Warrior (Arms): Improved Hamstring -> Hobble
-- ============================================================
-- TODO.md: "Improved Hamstring (Renamed to Hobble) (2, 5): Using Hamstring with
--           a two-handed weapon equipped increases your chance to parry by
--           3/6/10% for 10s. (3 ranks)"
--
-- Entirely DBC.  Two things make that possible:
--
-- 1. The talent is ALREADY a SPELL_AURA_PROC_TRIGGER_SPELL off Hamstring, and
--    core already ships exactly the spell_proc row this needs
--    (data/sql/base/db_world/spell_proc.sql:226):
--        (-12289, 0, 4, 2, 0,0, 0, 0, 2, 0, 0,0,0,0,0,0)
--    SpellFamilyName 4 with SpellFamilyMask0 = 0x2 is Hamstring 1715, and
--    SpellPhaseMask is already 2.  Only the payload changes, so that row is
--    deliberately left alone -- overriding it would risk widening the filter.
--    The stock ProcFlags (87376) are kept for the same reason; Hamstring is
--    DamageClass 2, so DONE_SPELL_MELEE_DMG_CLASS is already in that mask.
--
-- 2. The two-handed requirement needs no script.  EquippedItemClass /
--    EquippedItemSubClassMask on a PASSIVE spell are re-checked at proc time by
--    Aura::GetProcEffectMask (SpellAuras.cpp:2217-2254), which resolves the
--    weapon from damageInfo->GetAttackType().  Hamstring is a melee-damage-class
--    spell, so that is BASE_ATTACK -> mainhand.
--
--    Worth knowing, because it is not obvious: Hamstring deals no damage, but
--    the proc still carries a DamageInfo.  Spell::DoAllEffectOnTarget's
--    zero-damage branch (Spell.cpp:2890-2898) builds one with NODAMAGE and
--    passes it, so GetDamageInfo() is non-null and the item lookup works.  Had
--    it been null, line 2252 would have dropped the proc every single time.
--
-- SubClassMask 354 = 2H axe (0x2) | 2H mace (0x20) | polearm (0x40) |
-- 2H sword (0x100), matching Two-Handed Weapon Specialization 12163.  Staves
-- are excluded, as they are there.
--
-- ProcChance goes 5/10/15 -> 100: the redesign has no chance clause, the rank
-- scaling moved into the payload.
--
-- Rank 3 (23695) also gets DurationIndex 21 to match ranks 1 and 2; it ships
-- with 0, which is a stock inconsistency rather than a deliberate difference.
--
-- Spells:
--   12289 / 12668 / 23695 = Hobble ranks 1-3 (the talent)
--   200620 / 200621 / 200622 = the 3 / 6 / 10% parry buffs, 10 sec
-- The stock root trigger 23694 is simply no longer referenced.
-- ============================================================

-- ============================================================
-- 200620-200622: the parry buffs
-- ============================================================
-- Cloned from Deflection rank 1 (16462) rather than a rogue spell, because it
-- is already SPELL_AURA_MOD_PARRY_PERCENT with SpellFamilyName 0 and no class
-- masks or misc values to inherit -- there is nothing to scrub.
--
-- Attributes 0 (16462 has 464 = PASSIVE | DO_NOT_DISPLAY | DO_NOT_LOG): these
-- are real buffs and must be visible and castable.
-- DurationIndex 1 = 10000 ms.
-- Base points 2/5/9 render 3/6/10 under the N-1 convention.
--
-- Both SpellDescription0 and SpellToolTip0 are set.  The buff bar renders
-- SpellToolTip, so a visible aura with only a description has no hover text.

DELETE FROM `alonecraft_spell_dbc` WHERE `ID` IN (200620, 200621, 200622);
